x: 512 Expression -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The expression in the ta- ble calculation. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 4096 SortConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The sort configuration for a PivotTableVi- sual . FieldSortOptions -&gt; (list) The field sort options for a pivot table sort configuration. Constraints: o max: 200 (structure) The field sort options for a pivot table sort configuration. FieldId -&gt; (string) [required] The field ID for the field sort options. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 SortBy -&gt; (structure) [required] The sort by field for the field sort options. Field -&gt; (structure) The field sort (field id, di- rection) for the pivot table sort by options. FieldId -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The sort configuration target field. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 Direction -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The sort direction. Choose one of the following op- tions: o ASC : Ascending o DESC : Descending Possible values: o ASC o DESC Column -&gt; (structure) The column sort (field id, direction) for the pivot ta- ble sort by options. SortBy -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] A column of a data set. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the col- umn. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Direction -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The sort direction. Possible values: o ASC o DESC AggregationFunction -&gt; (structure) The aggregation function that is defined in the column sort. NumericalAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for numer- ical values. SimpleNumericalAggre- gation -&gt; (string) Built-in aggrega- tion functions for numerical values. o SUM : The sum of a dimension or measure. o AVERAGE : The av- erage of a dimen- sion or measure. o MIN : The minimum value of a dimen- sion or measure. o MAX : The maximum value of a dimen- sion or measure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or measure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of dis- tinct values in a dimension or mea- sure. o VAR : The vari- ance of a dimen- sion or measure. o VARP : The parti- tioned variance of a dimension or measure. o STDEV : The stan- dard deviation of a dimension or measure. o STDEVP : The par- titioned standard deviation of a dimension or mea- sure. o MEDIAN : The me- dian value of a dimension or mea- sure. Possible values: o SUM o AVERAGE o MIN o MAX o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o VAR o VARP o STDEV o STDEVP o MEDIAN PercentileAggregation -&gt; (structure) An aggregation based on the per- centile of values in a dimension or measure. PercentileValue -&gt; (double) The percentile value. This value can be any numeric constant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the median value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 CategoricalAggregation- Function -&gt; (string) Aggregation for cate- gorical values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Ag- gregate by the total number of distinct values. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT DateAggregationFunction -&gt; (string) Aggregation for date values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Ag- gregate by the total number of distinct values. o MIN : Select the smallest date value. o MAX : Select the largest date value. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o MIN o MAX AttributeAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for at- tributes. SimpleAttributeAggre- gation -&gt; (string) The built-in aggre- gation functions for attributes. o UNIQUE_VALUE : Returns the unique value for a field, aggre- gated by the di- mension fields. Possible values: o UNIQUE_VALUE ValueForMultipleValues -&gt; (string) Used by the UNIQUE_VALUE aggre- gation function. If there are multiple values for the field used by the aggregation, the value for this property will be returned instead.