nstant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the median value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 CategoricalAggregation- Function -&gt; (string) Aggregation for cate- gorical values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Ag- gregate by the total number of distinct values. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT DateAggregationFunction -&gt; (string) Aggregation for date values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Ag- gregate by the total number of distinct values. o MIN : Select the smallest date value. o MAX : Select the largest date value. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o MIN o MAX AttributeAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for at- tributes. SimpleAttributeAggre- gation -&gt; (string) The built-in aggre- gation functions for attributes. o UNIQUE_VALUE : Returns the unique value for a field, aggre- gated by the di- mension fields. Possible values: o UNIQUE_VALUE ValueForMultipleValues -&gt; (string) Used by the UNIQUE_VALUE aggre- gation function. If there are multiple values for the field used by the aggregation, the value for this property will be returned instead. Defaults to '*'. TooltipTarget -&gt; (string) Determines the target of the column tooltip item in a combo chart visual. Possible values: o BOTH o BAR o LINE SheetTooltip -&gt; (structure) The configuration of the sheet tooltip. SheetId -&gt; (string) The sheet ID of the tooltip sheet that is used by the tooltip. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ ReferenceLines -&gt; (list) The reference line setup of the visual. Constraints: o max: 20 (structure) The reference line visual display op- tions. Status -&gt; (string) The status of the reference line. Choose one of the following options: o ENABLE o DISABLE Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED DataConfiguration -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] The data configuration of the refer- ence line. StaticConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The static data configuration of the reference line data configu- ration. Value -&gt; (double) [required] The double input of the sta- tic data. DynamicConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The dynamic configuration of the reference line data configura- tion. Column -&gt; (structure) [required] The column that the dynamic data targets. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the col- umn belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The name of the column. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 MeasureAggregationFunction -&gt; (structure) The aggregation function that is used in the dynamic data. NumericalAggregationFunction -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for numerical values. SimpleNumericalAggregation -&gt; (string) Built-in aggregation functions for numeri- cal values. o SUM : The sum of a dimension or mea- sure. o AVERAGE : The aver- age of a dimension or measure. o MIN : The minimum value of a dimension or measure. o MAX : The maximum value of a dimension or measure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or mea- sure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of distinct values in a dimen- sion or measure. o VAR : The variance of a dimension or measure. o VARP : The parti- tioned variance of a dimension or mea- sure. o STDEV : The standard deviation of a di- mension or measure. o STDEVP : The parti- tioned standard de- viation of a dimen- sion or measure. o MEDIAN : The median value of a dimension or measure. Possible values: o SUM o AVERAGE o MIN o MAX o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o VAR o VARP o STDEV o STDEVP o MEDIAN PercentileAggregation -&gt; (structure) An aggregation based on the percentile of values in a dimension or measure. PercentileValue -&gt; (double) The percentile value. This value can be any numeric constant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the me- dian value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 CategoricalAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (string) Aggregation for categori- cal values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Aggre- gate by the total number of distinct values. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT DateAggregationFunction -&gt; (string) Aggregation for date val- ues. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Aggre- gate by the total number of distinct values. o MIN : Select the small- est date value. o MAX : Select the largest date value. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o MIN o MAX AttributeAggregationFunction -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for attrib- utes. SimpleAttributeAggregation -&gt; (string) The built-in aggrega- tion functions for at- tributes. o UNIQUE_VALUE : Re- turns the unique value for a field, aggregated by the dimension fields. Possible values: o UNIQUE_VALUE ValueForMultipleValues -&gt; (string) Used by the UNIQUE_VALUE aggrega- tion function. If there are multiple values for the field used by the aggrega- tion, the value for this property will be returned instead. De- faults to '*'. Calculation -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] The calculation that is used in the dynamic data. SimpleNumericalAggregation -&gt; (string) Built-in aggregation func- tions for numerical val- ues. o SUM : The sum of a di- mension or measure. o AVERAGE : The average of a dimension or measure. o MIN : The minimum value of a dimension or mea- sure. o MAX : The maximum value of a dimension or mea- sure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or measure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of distinct values in a dimension or mea- sure. o VAR : The variance of a dimension or measure. o VARP : The partitioned variance of a dimension or measure. o STDEV : The standard de- viation of a dimension or measure. o STDEVP : The partitioned standard deviation of a dimension or measure. o MEDIAN : The median value of a dimension or measure. P