al. This identi- fier must be unique within the context of a dashboard, template, or analysis. Two dash- boards, analyses, or templates can have visuals with the same identifiers. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Title -&gt; (structure) The title that is displayed on the visual. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the title label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE FormatText -&gt; (structure) The short text format of the title label, such as plain text or rich text. PlainText -&gt; (string) Plain text format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 RichText -&gt; (string) Rich text. Examples of rich text include bold, underline, and italics. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1024 Subtitle -&gt; (structure) The subtitle that is displayed on the visual. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the subtitle label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE FormatText -&gt; (structure) The long text format of the subtitle label, such as plain text or rich text. PlainText -&gt; (string) Plain text format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1024 RichText -&gt; (string) Rich text. Examples of rich text include bold, underline, and italics. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ChartConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The configuration of a GaugeChartVisual . FieldWells -&gt; (structure) The field well configuration of a GaugeChartVisual . Values -&gt; (list) The value field wells of a GaugeChartVi- sual . Constraints: o max: 200 (structure) The measure (metric) type field. NumericalMeasureField -&gt; (structure) The measure type field with nu- merical type columns. FieldId -&gt; (string) [required] The custom field ID. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 Column -&gt; (structure) [required] The column that is used in the NumericalMeasureField . DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the col- umn belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The name of the column. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 AggregationFunction -&gt; (struc- ture) The aggregation function of the measure field. SimpleNumericalAggregation -&gt; (string) Built-in aggregation func- tions for numerical val- ues. o SUM : The sum of a di- mension or measure. o AVERAGE : The average of a dimension or measure. o MIN : The minimum value of a dimension or mea- sure. o MAX : The maximum value of a dimension or mea- sure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or measure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of distinct values in a dimension or mea- sure. o VAR : The variance of a dimension or measure. o VARP : The partitioned variance of a dimension or measure. o STDEV : The standard de- viation of a dimension or measure. o STDEVP : The partitioned standard deviation of a dimension or measure. o MEDIAN : The median value of a dimension or measure. Possible values: o SUM o AVERAGE o MIN o MAX o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o VAR o VARP o STDEV o STDEVP o MEDIAN PercentileAggregation -&gt; (structure) An aggregation based on the percentile of values in a dimension or measure. PercentileValue -&gt; (dou- ble) The percentile value. This value can be any numeric constant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the median value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 FormatConfiguration -&gt; (struc- ture) The format configuration of the field. FormatConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the numeric format config- uration. NumberDisplayFormatConfig- uration -&gt; (structure) The options that de- termine the number display format config- uration. Prefix -&gt; (string) Determines the pre- fix value of the number format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Suffix -&gt; (string) Determines the suf- fix value of the number format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 SeparatorConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the nu- meric separator configuration. DecimalSeparator -&gt; (string) Determines the decimal separa-