tion of the column tooltip item. NumericalAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for numer- ical values. SimpleNumericalAggre- gation -&gt; (string) Built-in aggrega- tion functions for numerical values. o SUM : The sum of a dimension or measure. o AVERAGE : The av- erage of a dimen- sion or measure. o MIN : The minimum value of a dimen- sion or measure. o MAX : The maximum value of a dimen- sion or measure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or measure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of dis- tinct values in a dimension or mea- sure. o VAR : The vari- ance of a dimen- sion or measure. o VARP : The parti- tioned variance of a dimension or measure. o STDEV : The stan- dard deviation of a dimension or measure. o STDEVP : The par- titioned standard deviation of a dimension or mea- sure. o MEDIAN : The me- dian value of a dimension or mea- sure. Possible values: o SUM o AVERAGE o MIN o MAX o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o VAR o VARP o STDEV o STDEVP o MEDIAN PercentileAggregation -&gt; (structure) An aggregation based on the per- centile of values in a dimension or measure. PercentileValue -&gt; (double) The percentile value. This value can be any numeric constant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the median value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 CategoricalAggregation- Function -&gt; (string) Aggregation for cate- gorical values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Ag- gregate by the total number of distinct values. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT DateAggregationFunction -&gt; (string) Aggregation for date values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Ag- gregate by the total number of distinct values. o MIN : Select the smallest date value. o MAX : Select the largest date value. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o MIN o MAX AttributeAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for at- tributes. SimpleAttribute