regation function that is defined in the column sort. NumericalAggregationFunction -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for numerical values. SimpleNumericalAggregation -&gt; (string) Built-in aggregation functions for numeri- cal values. o SUM : The sum of a dimension or mea- sure. o AVERAGE : The aver- age of a dimension or measure. o MIN : The minimum value of a dimension or measure. o MAX : The maximum value of a dimension or measure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or mea- sure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of distinct values in a dimen- sion or measure. o VAR : The variance of a dimension or measure. o VARP : The parti- tioned variance of a dimension or mea- sure. o STDEV : The standard deviation of a di- mension or measure. o STDEVP : The parti- tioned standard de- viation of a dimen- sion or measure. o MEDIAN : The median value of a dimension or measure. Possible values: o SUM o AVERAGE o MIN o MAX o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o VAR o VARP o STDEV o STDEVP o MEDIAN PercentileAggregation -&gt; (structure) An aggregation based on the percentile of values in a dimension or measure. PercentileValue -&gt; (double) The percentile value. This value can be any numeric constant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the me- dian value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 CategoricalAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (string) Aggregation for categori- cal values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Aggre- gate by the total number of distinct values. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT DateAggregationFunction -&gt; (string) Aggregation for date val- ues. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Aggre- gate by the total number of distinct values. o MIN : Select the small- est date value. o MAX : Select the largest date value. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o MIN o MAX AttributeAggregationFunction -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for attrib- utes. SimpleAttributeAggregation -&gt; (string) The built-in aggrega- tion functions for at- tributes. o UNIQUE_VALUE : Re- turns the unique value for a field, aggregated by the dimension fields. Possible values: o UNIQUE_VALUE ValueForMultipleValues -&gt; (string) Used by the UNIQUE_VALUE aggrega- tion function. If there are multiple values for the field used by the aggrega- tion, the value for this property will be returned instead. De- faults to '*'. CategoryItemsLimit -&gt; (structure) The limit on the number of categories displayed. ItemsLimit -&gt; (long) The limit on how many items of a field are showed in the chart. For example, the number of slices that are displayed in a pie chart. OtherCategories -&gt; (string) The Show other of an axis in the chart. Choose one of the following options: o INCLUDE o EXCLUDE Possible values: o INCLUDE o EXCLUDE CategoryLabelOptions -&gt; (structure) The label options of the categories that are displayed in a FunnelChartVisual . Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of an axis label on a chart. Choose one of the following op- tions: o VISIBLE : Shows the axis. o HIDDEN : Hides the axis. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE SortIconVisibility -&gt; (string) The visibility configuration of the sort icon on a chart's axis label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE AxisLabelOptions -&gt; (list) The label options for a chart axis. Constraints: o max: 100 (structure) The label options for a chart axis. You must specify the field that the label is targeted to. FontConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The font configuration of the axis label. FontSize -&gt; (structure) The option that determines the text display size. Relative -&gt; (string) The lexical name for the text size, proportional to its surrounding context. Possible values: o EXTRA_SMALL o SMALL o MEDIUM o LARGE o EXTRA_LARGE Absolute -&gt; (string) The font size that you want to use in px. FontDecoration -&gt; (string) Determines the appearance of decorative lines on the text. Possible values: o UNDERLINE o NONE FontColor -&gt; (string) Determines the color of the text. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}$ FontWeight -&gt; (structure) The option that determines the text display weight, or boldness. Name -&gt; (string) The lexical name for the level of boldness of the text display. Possible values: o NORMAL o BOLD FontStyle -&gt; (string) Determines the text display face that is inherited by the given font family. Possible values: o NORMAL o ITALIC FontFamily -&gt; (string) The font family that you want to use. Constraints: o max: 256 CustomLabel -&gt; (string) The text for the axis label. ApplyTo -&gt; (structure) The options that indicate which field the label belongs to. FieldId -&gt; (string) [required] The field that the axis label is targeted to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 Column -&gt; (structure) [required] The column that the axis la- bel is targeted to. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the col- umn belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The name of the column. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 ValueLabelOptions -&gt; (structure) The label options for the values that are displayed in a FunnelChartVisual . Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of an axis label on a chart. Choose one of the following op- tions: o VISIBLE : Shows the axis. o HIDDEN : Hides the axis. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE SortIconVisibility -&gt; (string) The visibility configuration of the sort icon on a chart's axis label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE AxisLabelOptions -&gt; (list) The label options for a chart axis. Constraints: o max: 100 (structure) The label options for a chart axis. You must specify the field that the label is targeted to. FontConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The font configuration of the axis label. FontSize -&gt; (structure) The option that determines the text