sion or measure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or mea- sure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of distinct values in a dimen- sion or measure. o VAR : The variance of a dimension or measure. o VARP : The parti- tioned variance of a dimension or mea- sure. o STDEV : The standard deviation of a di- mension or measure. o STDEVP : The parti- tioned standard de- viation of a dimen- sion or measure. o MEDIAN : The median value of a dimension or measure. Possible values: o SUM o AVERAGE o MIN o MAX o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o VAR o VARP o STDEV o STDEVP o MEDIAN PercentileAggregation -&gt; (structure) An aggregation based on the percentile of values in a dimension or measure. PercentileValue -&gt; (double) The percentile value. This value can be any numeric constant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the me- dian value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 FormatConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The format configuration of the field. FormatConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The options that de- termine the numeric format configuration. NumberDisplayFormat- Configuration -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the num- ber display format configuration. Prefix -&gt; (string) Determines the prefix value of the number for- mat. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Suffix -&gt; (string) Determines the suffix value of the number for- mat. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 SeparatorConfigura- tion -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the numeric separator con- figuration. DecimalSepara- tor -&gt; (string) Determines the decimal separator. Possible values: o COMMA o DOT o SPACE ThousandsSepa- rator -&gt; (structure) The options that deter- mine the thousands separator configura- tion. Symbol -&gt; (string) Deter- mines the thou- sands separa- tor sym- bol. Possible values: o COMMA o DOT o SPACE Visibility -&gt; (string) Deter- mines the vis- ibility of the thou- sands separa- tor. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISI- BLE Group- ingStyle -&gt; (string) Deter- mines t