raints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the col- umn. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Direction -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The sort direction. Possible values: o ASC o DESC AggregationFunction -&gt; (structure) The aggregation function that is defined in the column sort. NumericalAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for numer- ical values. SimpleNumericalAggre- gation -&gt; (string) Built-in aggrega- tion functions for numerical values. o SUM : The sum of a dimension or measure. o AVERAGE : The av- erage of a dimen- sion or measure. o MIN : The minimum value of a dimen- sion or measure. o MAX : The maximum value of a dimen- sion or measure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or measure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of dis- tinct values in a dimension or mea- sure. o VAR : The vari- ance of a dimen- sion or measure. o VARP : The parti- tioned variance of a dimension or measure. o STDEV : The stan- dard deviation of a dimension or measure. o STDEVP : The par- titioned standard deviation of a dimension or mea- sure. o MEDIAN : The me- dian value of a dimension or mea- sure. Possible values: o SUM o AVERAGE o MIN o MAX o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o VAR o VARP o STDEV o STDEVP o MEDIAN PercentileAggregation -&gt; (structure) An aggregation based on the per- centile of values in a dimension or measure. PercentileValue -&gt; (double) The percentile value. This value can be any numeric constant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the median value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 CategoricalAggregation- Function -&gt; (string) Aggregation for cate- gorical values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Ag- gregate by the total number of distinct values. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT DateAggregationFunction -&gt; (string) Aggregation for date values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Ag- gregate by the total number of distinct values. o MIN : Select the smallest date value. o MAX : Select the largest date value. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o MIN o MAX AttributeAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for at- tributes. SimpleAttributeAggre- gation -&gt; (string) The built-in aggre- gation functions for attributes. o UNIQUE_VALUE : Returns the unique value for a field, aggre- gated by the di- mension fields. Possible values: o UNIQUE_VALUE ValueForMultipleValues -&gt; (string) Used by the UNIQUE_VALUE aggre- gation function. If there are multiple values for the field used by the aggregation, the value for this property will be returned instead. Defaults to '*'. ItemsLimitConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The maximum amount of data to be re- turned by a query. ItemsLimit -&gt; (long) Determines how many values are be fetched at once. Actions -&gt; (list) The list of custom actions that are configured for a visual. Constraints: o max: 10 (structure) A custom action defined on a visual. CustomActionId -&gt; (string) [required] The ID of the VisualCustomAction . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the VisualCustomAction . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 256 Status -&gt; (string) The status of the VisualCustomAction . Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED Trigger -&gt; (string) [required] The trigger of the VisualCustomAction . Valid values are defined as follows: o DATA_POINT_CLICK : Initiates a custom action by a left pointer click on a data point. o DATA_POINT_MENU : Initiates a custom action by right pointer click from the menu. Possible values: o DATA_POINT_CLICK o DATA_POINT_MENU ActionOperations -&gt; (list) [required] A list of VisualCustomActionOperations . This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2 (structure) The operation that is defined by the custom action. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. FilterOperation -&gt; (structure) The filter operation that filters data included in a visual or in an entire sheet. SelectedFieldsConfiguration -&gt; (structure) [required] The configuration that chooses the fields to be fil- tered. SelectedFields -&gt; (list) Chooses the fields that are filtered in CustomAc- tionFilterOperation . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 20 (string) Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 SelectedFieldOptions -&gt; (string) A structure that contains the options that choose which fields are filtered in the CustomActionFilter- Operation . Valid values are defined as follows: o ALL_FIELDS : Applies the filter operation to all fields. Possible values: o ALL_FIELDS SelectedColumns -&gt; (list) The selected columns of a dataset. Constraints: o max: 10 (structure) A column of a data set. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the column. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 TargetVisualsConfiguration -&gt; (structure) [required] The configuration that chooses the target visuals to be filtered. SameSheetTargetVisualConfigu- ration -&gt; (structure) The configuration of the same-sheet target visuals that you want to be fil- tered. TargetVisuals -&gt; (list) A list of the target visual IDs that are located in the same sheet of the analysis. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 75 (string) Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ TargetVisualOptions -&gt; (string) The options that choose the target vi- sual in the same sheet. Valid values are de- fined as follows: o ALL_VISUALS : Ap- plies the filter op- eration to all visu- als in the same sheet. Possible values: o ALL_VISUALS NavigationOperation -&gt; (structure) The navigation operation that navigates between different sheets in the same analysis. LocalNavigationConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The configuration that chooses the navigation tar- get. TargetSheetId -&gt; (string) [required] The sheet that is targeted for navigation in the same analysis. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ URLOperation -&gt; (structure) The URL operation that opens a link to another webpage. URLTemplate -&gt; (string) [re- quired] THe URL link of the CustomAc- tionURLOperation . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 URLTarget -&gt; (string) [required] The target of the CustomAc- tionURLOperation . Valid values are defined as follows: o NEW_TAB : Opens the target URL in a new browser tab. o NEW_WINDOW : Opens the tar- get URL in a new browser window. o SAME_TAB : Opens the target URL in the same browser tab. Possible values: o NEW_TAB o NEW_WINDOW o SAME_TAB SetParametersOperation -&gt; (struc- ture) The set parameter operation that sets parameters in custom action. ParameterValueConfigurations -&gt; (list) [required] The parameter that determines the value configuration. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 200 (structure) The configuration of adding parameters in ac- tion. DestinationParameterName -&gt; (string) [required] The destination para- meter name of the Set- ParameterValueConfigu- ration . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 o pattern: ^[a-zA-Z0-9]+$ Value -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] The configuration of destination parameter values. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the at- tributes can be de- fined. CustomValuesConfigura- tion -&gt; (structure) The configuration of custom values for destination pa- rameter in Destina- tionParameterValue- Configuration . IncludeNullValue -&gt; (boolean) Includes the null value in custom action parameter val- ues. CustomValues -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] The customized parameter val- ues. This is a union type structure. For this struc- ture to be valid, only one of the attrib- utes can be de- fined. StringValues -&gt; (list) A list of string-type parameter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (string) IntegerValues -&gt; (list) A list of integer-type parameter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (long) DecimalValues -&gt; (list) A list of decimal-type parameter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (double) DateTimeValues -&gt; (list) A list of date- time-type parameter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (timestamp) SelectAllValueOptions -&gt; (string) The configuration that selects all options. Possible values: o ALL_VALUES SourceParameterName -&gt; (string) The source parame- ter name of the destination parame- ter. SourceField -&gt; (string) The source field ID of the destination parameter. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 SourceColumn -&gt; (structure) A column of a data set. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column be- longs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the column. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 VisualContentAltText -&gt; (string) The alt text for the visual. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1024 TextBoxes -&gt; (list) The text boxes that are on a sheet. Constraints: o max: 100 (structure) A text box. SheetTextBoxId -&gt; (string) [required] The unique identifier for a text box. This identi- fier must be unique within the context of a dash- board, template, or analysis. Two dashboards, analyses, or templates can have text boxes that share identifiers. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Content -&gt; (string) The content that is displayed in the text box. Constraints: o max: 150000 Interactions -&gt; (structure) The general textbox interactions setup for a textbox. TextBoxMenuOption -&gt; (structure) The menu options for the textbox. AvailabilityStatus -&gt; 