ption -&gt; (structure) The menu options for the image. AvailabilityStatus -&gt; (string) The availability status of the image menu. If the value of this property is set to EN- ABLED , dashboard readers can interact with the image menu. Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED Actions -&gt; (list) A list of custom actions that are configured for an image. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 10 (structure) A custom action defined on an image. CustomActionId -&gt; (string) [required] The ID of the custom action. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the custom action. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 256 Status -&gt; (string) The status of the custom action. Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED Trigger -&gt; (string) [required] The trigger of the VisualCustomAction . Valid values are defined as follows: o CLICK : Initiates a custom action by a left pointer click on a data point. o MENU : Initiates a custom action by right pointer click from the menu. Possible values: o CLICK o MENU ActionOperations -&gt; (list) [required] A list of ImageCustomActionOperations . This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the at- tributes can be defined. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2 (structure) The operation that is defined by the custom action. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. NavigationOperation -&gt; (structure) The navigation operation that navi- gates between different sheets in the same analysis. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. LocalNavigationConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The configuration that chooses the navigation target. TargetSheetId -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The sheet that is targeted for navigation in the same analysis. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ URLOperation -&gt; (structure) The URL operation that opens a link to another webpage. URLTemplate -&gt; (string) [required] THe URL link of the CustomAc- tionURLOperation . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 URLTarget -&gt; (string) [required] The target of the CustomActionUR- LOperation . Valid values are defined as fol- lows: o NEW_TAB : Opens the target URL in a new browser tab. o NEW_WINDOW : Opens the target URL in a new browser window. o SAME_TAB : Opens the target URL in the same browser tab. Possible values: o NEW_TAB o NEW_WINDOW o SAME_TAB SetParametersOperation -&gt; (structure) The set parameter operation that sets parameters in custom action. ParameterValueConfigurations -&gt; (list) [required] The parameter that determines the value configuration. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 200 (structure) The configuration of adding parameters in action. DestinationParameterName -&gt; (string) [required] The destination parameter name of the SetParameter- ValueConfiguration . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 o pattern: ^[a-zA-Z0-9]+$ Value -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] The configuration of des- tination parameter values. This is a union type structure. For this struc- ture to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. CustomValuesConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The configuration of custom values for des- tination parameter in DestinationParameter- ValueConfiguration . IncludeNullValue -&gt; (boolean) Includes the null value in custom ac- tion parameter val- ues. CustomValues -&gt; (structure) [required] The customized pa- rameter values. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. StringValues -&gt; (list) A list of string-type pa- rameter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (string) IntegerValues -&gt; (list) A list of inte- ger-type para- meter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (long) DecimalValues -&gt; (list) A list of deci- mal-type para- meter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (double) DateTimeValues -&gt; (list) A list of date- time-type para- meter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (timestamp) SelectAllValueOptions -&gt; (string) The configuration that selects all options. Possible values: o ALL_VALUES SourceParameterName -&gt; (string) The source parameter name of the destina- tion parameter. SourceField -&gt; (string) The source field ID of the destination para- meter. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 SourceColumn -&gt; (struc- ture) A column of a data set. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the column. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Layouts -&gt; (list) Layouts define how the components of a sheet are arranged. For more information, see Types of layout in the Amazon Quick Suite User Guide . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1 (structure) A Layout defines the placement of elements within a sheet. For more information, see Types of layout in the Ama- zon Quick Suite User Guide . This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. Configuration -&gt; (structure) [required] The configuration that determines what the type of layout for a sheet. GridLayout -&gt; (structure) A type of layout that can be used on a sheet. In a grid layout, visuals snap to a grid with standard spacing and alignment. Dashboards are displayed as designed, with options to fit to screen or view at actual size. A grid layout can be configured to behave in one of two ways when the viewport is resized: FIXED or RESPON- SIVE . Elements -&gt; (list) [required] The elements that are included in a grid layout. Constraints: o max: 430 (structure) An element within a grid layout. ElementId -&gt; (string) [required] A unique identifier for an element within a grid layout. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ ElementType -&gt; (string) [required] The type of element. Possible values: o VISUAL o FILTER_CONTROL o PARAMETER_CONTROL o TEXT_BOX o IMAGE ColumnIndex -&gt; (integer) The column index for the upper left corner of an element. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 35 ColumnSpan -&gt; (integer) [required] The width of a grid element ex- pressed as a number of grid columns. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 36 RowIndex -&gt; (integer) The row index for the upper left corner of an element. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 9009 RowSpan -&gt; (integer) [required] The height of a grid element ex- pressed as a number of grid rows. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 21 BorderStyle -&gt; (structure) The border style configuration of a grid layout element. Visibility -&gt; (string) The border visibility of a grid layout element. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE Color -&gt; (string) The border color of a grid layout element. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}(?:[A-F0-9]{2})?$ Width -&gt; (string) The border width of a grid layout element. Constraints: o max: 50 SelectedBorderStyle -&gt; (structure) The border style configuration of a grid layout element. This border style is used when the element is selected. Visibility -&gt; (string) The border visibility of a grid layout element. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE Color -&gt; (string) The border color of a grid layout element. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}(?:[A-F0-9]{2})?$ Width -&gt; (string) The border width of a grid layout element. Constraints: o max: 50 BackgroundStyle -&gt; (structure) The background style configuration of a grid layout element. Visibility -&gt; (string) The background visibility of a grid layout element. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE Color -&gt; (string) The background color of a grid layout element. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}(?:[A-F0-9]{2})?$ LoadingAnimation -&gt; (structure) The configuration of loading anima- tion in free-form layout. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility configuration of LoadingAnimation . Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE BorderRadius -&gt; (string) The border radius of a grid layout element. Constraints: o max: 50 Padding -&gt; (string) The padding of a grid layout ele- ment. Constraints: o max: 200 CanvasSizeOptions -&gt; (structure) Configuration options for the canvas of a grid layout. ScreenCanvasSizeOptions -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the sizing of the canvas used in a grid layout. ResizeOption -&gt; (string) [required] This value determines the layout be- havior when the viewport is resized. o FIXED : A fixed width will be used when optimizing the layout. In the Quick Sight console, this option is called Classic . o RESPONSIVE : The width of the can- vas will be responsive and opti- mized to the view port. In the Quick Sight console, this option is called Tiled . Possible values: o FIXED o RESPONSIVE OptimizedViewPortWidth -&gt; (string) The width that the view port will be optimized for when the layout ren- ders. FreeFormLayout -&gt; (structure) A free-form is optimized for a fixed width and has more control over the exact placement of layout elements. Elements -&gt; (list) [required] The elements that are included in a free-form layout. Constraints: o max: 430 (structure) An element within a free-form layout. ElementId -&gt; (string) [required] A unique identifier for an element within a free-form layout. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ ElementType -&gt; (string) [required] The type of element. Possible values: o VISUAL o FILTER_CONTROL o PARAMETER_CONTROL o TEXT_BOX o IMAGE XAxisLocation -&gt; (string) [required] The x-axis coordinate of the ele- ment. YAxisLocation -&gt; (string) [required] The y-axis coordinate of the ele- ment. Width -&gt; (string) [required] The width of an element within a free-form layout. Height -&gt; (string) [required] The height of an element within a free-form layout. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of an element within a free-form layout. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE RenderingRules -&gt; (list) The r