f a grid layout element. Visibility -&gt; (string) The border visibility of a grid layout element. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE Color -&gt; (string) The border color of a grid layout element. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}(?:[A-F0-9]{2})?$ Width -&gt; (string) The border width of a grid layout element. Constraints: o max: 50 SelectedBorderStyle -&gt; (structure) The border style configuration of a grid layout element. This border style is used when the element is selected. Visibility -&gt; (string) The border visibility of a grid layout element. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE Color -&gt; (string) The border color of a grid layout element. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}(?:[A-F0-9]{2})?$ Width -&gt; (string) The border width of a grid layout element. Constraints: o max: 50 BackgroundStyle -&gt; (structure) The background style configuration of a grid layout element. Visibility -&gt; (string) The background visibility of a grid layout element. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE Color -&gt; (string) The background color of a grid layout element. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}(?:[A-F0-9]{2})?$ LoadingAnimation -&gt; (structure) The configuration of loading anima- tion in free-form layout. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility configuration of LoadingAnimation . Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE BorderRadius -&gt; (string) The border radius of a grid layout element. Constraints: o max: 50 Padding -&gt; (string) The padding of a grid layout ele- ment. Constraints: o max: 200 CanvasSizeOptions -&gt; (structure) Configuration options for the canvas of a grid layout. ScreenCanvasSizeOptions -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the sizing of the canvas used in a grid layout. ResizeOption -&gt; (string) [required] This value determines the layout be- havior when the viewport is resized. o FIXED : A fixed width will be used when optimizing the layout. In the Quick Sight console, this option is called Classic . o RESPONSIVE : The width of the can- vas will be responsive and opti- mized to the view port. In the Quick Sight console, this option is called Tiled . Possible values: o FIXED o RESPONSIVE OptimizedViewPortWidth -&gt; (string) The width that the view port will be optimized for when the layout ren- ders. ContentType -&gt; (string) The layout content type of the sheet. Choose one of the following options: o PAGINATED : Creates a sheet for a paginated report. o INTERACTIVE : Creates a sheet for an interactive dash- board. Possible values: o PAGINATED o INTERACTIVE CustomActionDefaults -&gt; (structure) A list of visual custom actions for the sheet. highlightOperation -&gt; (structure) A list of highlight operations available for visuals in an analysis or sheet. Trigger -&gt; (string) [required] Specifies whether a highlight operation is initi- ated by a click or hover, or whether it's dis- abled. Possible values: o DATA_POINT_CLICK o DATA_POINT_HOVER o NONE TooltipSheets -&gt; (list) An array of tooltip sheet definitions for a dashboard. Constraints: o max: 50 (structure) A tooltip sheet is an object that contains a set of visuals that are used as a tooltip. Every analysis and dashboard must contain at least one non-tooltip sheet. SheetId -&gt; (string) [required] The unique identifier of a tooltip sheet. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Name -&gt; (string) The name of the tooltip sheet. This name is displayed on the sheet's tab in the Quick console. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 Visuals -&gt; (list) A list of the visuals that are on a tooltip sheet. Constraints: o max: 5 (structure) A visual displayed on a sheet in an analysis, dash- board, or template. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. TableVisual -&gt; (structure) A table visual. For more information, see Using tables as visuals in the Amazon Quick Suite User Guide . VisualId -&gt; (string) [required] The unique identifier of a visual. This identi- fier must be unique within the context of a dashboard, template, or analysis. Two dash- boards, analyses, or templates can have visuals with the same identifiers.. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Title -&gt; (structure) The title that is displayed on the visual. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the title label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE FormatText -&gt; (structure) The short text format of the title label, such as plain text or rich text. PlainText -&gt; (string) Plain text format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 RichText -&gt; (string) Rich text. Examples of rich text include bold, underline, and italics. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1024 Subtitle -&gt; (structure) The subtitle that is displayed on the visual. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the subtitle label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE FormatText -&gt; (structure) The long text format of the subtitle label, such as plain text or rich text. PlainText -&gt; (string) Plain text format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1024 RichText -&gt; (string) Rich text. Examples of rich text include bold, underline, and italics. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ChartConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The configuration settings of the visual. FieldWells -&gt; (structure) The field wells of the visual. TableAggregatedFieldWells -&gt; (structure) The aggregated field well for the table. GroupBy -&gt; (list) The group by field well for a pivot table. Values are grouped by group by fields. Constraints: o max: 200 (structure) The dimension type field. NumericalDimensionField -&gt; (structure) The dimension type field with numerical type columns. FieldId -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The custom field ID. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 Column -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] The column that is used in the NumericalDimension- Field . DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The to