ype of the ref- erence line. Choose one of the following options: o PrimaryY o SecondaryY Possible values: o PRIMARY_YAXIS o SECONDARY_YAXIS SeriesType -&gt; (string) The series type of the reference line data configuration. Choose one of the following options: o BAR o LINE Possible values: o BAR o LINE StyleConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The style configuration of the ref- erence line. Pattern -&gt; (string) The pattern type of the line style. Choose one of the follow- ing options: o SOLID o DASHED o DOTTED Possible values: o SOLID o DASHED o DOTTED Color -&gt; (string) The hex color of the reference line. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}$ LabelConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The label configuration of the ref- erence line. ValueLabelConfiguration -&gt; (struc- ture) The value label configuration of the label in a reference line. RelativePosition -&gt; (string) The relative position of the value label. Choose one of the following options: o BEFORE_CUSTOM_LABEL o AFTER_CUSTOM_LABEL Possible values: o BEFORE_CUSTOM_LABEL o AFTER_CUSTOM_LABEL FormatConfiguration -&gt; (struc- ture) The format configuration of the value label. NumberDisplayFormatConfigura- tion -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the number display format configuration. Prefix -&gt; (string) Determines the prefix value of the number format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Suffix -&gt; (string) Determines the suffix value of the number format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 SeparatorConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The options that de- termine the numeric separator configura- tion. DecimalSeparator -&gt; (string) Determines the dec- imal separator. Possible values: o COMMA o DOT o SPACE ThousandsSeparator -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the thou- sands separator configuration. Symbol -&gt; (string) Determines the thousands sepa- rator symbol. Possible val- ues: o COMMA o DOT o SPACE Visibility -&gt; (string) Determines the visibility of the thousands separator. Possible val- ues: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE GroupingStyle -&gt; (string) Determines the way numbers are styled to ac- commodate dif- ferent read- ability stan- dards. The DE- FAULT value uses the stan- dard interna- tional grouping system and groups numbers by the thou- sands. The LAKHS value uses the Indian numbering sys- tem and groups numbers by lakhs and crores. Possible val- ues: o DEFAULT o LAKHS DecimalPlacesConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The option that deter- mines the decimal places configuration. DecimalPlaces -&gt; (long) [required] The values of the decimal places. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 20 NumberScale -&gt; (string) Determines the number scale value of the number format. Possible values: o NONE o AUTO o THOUSANDS o MILLIONS o BILLIONS o TRILLIONS o LAKHS o CRORES NegativeValueConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The options that de- termine the negative value configuration. DisplayMode -&gt; (string) [required] Determines the dis- play mode of the negative value con- figuration. Possible values: o POSITIVE o NEGATIVE NullValueFormatConfigura- tion -&gt; (structure) The options that de- termine the null value format configuration. NullString -&gt; (string) [required] Determines the null string of null val- ues. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 CurrencyDisplayFormatConfigu- ration -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the currency display for- mat configuration. Prefix -&gt; (string) Determines the prefix value of the currency format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Suffix -&gt; (string) Determines the suffix value of the currency format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 SeparatorConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The options that de- termine the numeric separator configura- tion. DecimalSeparator -&gt; (string) Determines the dec- imal separator. Possible values: o COMMA o DOT o SPACE ThousandsSeparator -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the thou- sands separator configuration. Symbol -&gt; (string) Determines the thousands sepa- rator symbol. Possible v