NT : The count of a dimension or measure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of distinct values in a dimension or mea- sure. o VAR : The variance of a dimension or measure. o VARP : The partitioned variance of a dimension or measure. o STDEV : The standard de- viation of a dimension or measure. o STDEVP : The partitioned standard deviation of a dimension or measure. o MEDIAN : The median value of a dimension or measure. Possible values: o SUM o AVERAGE o MIN o MAX o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o VAR o VARP o STDEV o STDEVP o MEDIAN PercentileAggregation -&gt; (structure) An aggregation based on the percentile of values in a dimension or measure. PercentileValue -&gt; (dou- ble) The percentile value. This value can be any numeric constant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the median value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 FormatConfiguration -&gt; (struc- ture) The format configuration of the field. FormatConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the numeric format config- uration. NumberDisplayFormatConfig- uration -&gt; (structure) The options that de- termine the number display format config- uration. Prefix -&gt; (string) Determines the pre- fix value of the number format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Suffix -&gt; (string) Determines the suf- fix value of the number format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 SeparatorConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the nu- meric separator configuration. DecimalSeparator -&gt; (string) Determines the decimal separa- tor. Possible val- ues: o COMMA o DOT o SPACE ThousandsSeparator -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the thousands separator con- figuration. Symbol -&gt; (string) Determines the thou- sands sepa- rator sym- bol. Possible values: o COMMA o DOT o SPACE Visibility -&gt; (string) Determines the visibil- ity of the thousands separator. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE GroupingStyle -&gt; (string) Determines the way num- bers are styled to accommodate diffe