um label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE Position -&gt; (string) Determines the position of the data la- bels. Possible values: o INSIDE o OUTSIDE o LEFT o TOP o BOTTOM o RIGHT LabelContent -&gt; (string) Determines the content of the data la- bels. Possible values: o VALUE o PERCENT o VALUE_AND_PERCENT LabelFontConfiguration -&gt; (structure) Determines the font configuration of the data labels. FontSize -&gt; (structure) The option that determines the text display size. Relative -&gt; (string) The lexical name for the text size, proportional to its sur- rounding context. Possible values: o EXTRA_SMALL o SMALL o MEDIUM o LARGE o EXTRA_LARGE Absolute -&gt; (string) The font size that you want to use in px. FontDecoration -&gt; (string) Determines the appearance of decora- tive lines on the text. Possible values: o UNDERLINE o NONE FontColor -&gt; (string) Determines the color of the text. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}$ FontWeight -&gt; (structure) The option that determines the text display weight, or boldness. Name -&gt; (string) The lexical name for the level of boldness of the text display. Possible values: o NORMAL o BOLD FontStyle -&gt; (string) Determines the text display face that is inherited by the given font family. Possible values: o NORMAL o ITALIC FontFamily -&gt; (string) The font family that you want to use. Constraints: o max: 256 LabelColor -&gt; (string) Determines the color of the data labels. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}$ Overlap -&gt; (string) Determines whether overlap is enabled or disabled for the data labels. Possible values: o DISABLE_OVERLAP o ENABLE_OVERLAP TotalsVisibility -&gt; (string) Determines the visibility of the total. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE Tooltip -&gt; (structure) The tooltip display setup of the visual. TooltipVisibility -&gt; (string) Determines whether or not the tooltip is visible. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE SelectedTooltipType -&gt; (string) The selected type for the tooltip. Choose one of the following options: o BASIC : A basic tooltip. o DETAILED : A detailed tooltip. Possible values: o BASIC o DETAILED o SHEET FieldBasedTooltip -&gt; (structure) The setup for the detailed tooltip. The tooltip setup is always saved. The dis- play type is decided based on the tooltip type. AggregationVisibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of Show aggregations . Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE TooltipTitleType -&gt; (string) The type for the &gt;tooltip title. Choose one of the following options: o NONE : Doesn't use the primary value as the title. o PRIMARY_VALUE : Uses primary value as the title. Possible values: o NONE o PRIMARY_VALUE TooltipFields -&gt; (list) The fields configuration in the tooltip. Constraints: o max: 100 (structure) The tooltip. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. FieldTooltipItem -&gt; (structure) The tooltip item for the fields. FieldId -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The unique ID of the field that is targeted by the tooltip. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 Label -&gt; (string) The label of the tooltip item. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the tooltip item. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE TooltipTarget -&gt; (string) Determines the target of the field tooltip item in a combo chart visual. Possible values: o BOTH o BAR o LINE ColumnTooltipItem -&gt; (structure) The tooltip item for the columns that are not part of a field well. Column -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] The target column of the tooltip item. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the col- umn. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Label -&gt; (string) The label of the tooltip item. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the tooltip item. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE Aggregation -&gt; (structure) The aggregation function of the column tooltip item. NumericalAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for numer- ical values. SimpleNumericalAggre- gation -&gt; (string) Built-in aggrega- tion functions for numerical values. o SUM : The sum of a dimension or measure. o AVERAGE : The av- erage of a dimen- sion or measure. o MIN : The minimum value of a dimen- sion or measure. o MAX : The maximum value of a dimen- sion or measure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or measure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of dis- tinct values in a dimension or mea- sure. o VAR : The vari- ance of a dimen- sion or measure. o VARP : The parti- tioned variance of a dimension or measure. o STDEV : The stan- dard deviation of a dimension or measure. o STDEVP : The par- titioned standard deviation of a dimension or mea- sure. o MEDIAN : The me- dian value of a dimension or mea- sure. Possible values: o SUM o AVERAGE o MIN o MAX o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o VAR o VARP o STDEV o STDEVP o MEDIAN PercentileAggregation -&gt; (structure) An aggregation based on the per- centile of values in a dimension or measure. PercentileValue -&gt; (double) The percentile value. This value can be any numeric constant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the median value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 CategoricalAggregation- Function -&gt; (string) Aggregation for cate- gorical values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Ag- gregate by the total number of distinct values. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT DateAggregationFunction -&gt; (string) Aggregation for date values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Ag- gregate by the total number of distinct values. o MIN : Select the smallest date value. o MAX : Select the largest date value. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o MIN o MAX AttributeAggregationFunc- tion -&