etTooltip -&gt; (structure) The configuration of the sheet tooltip. SheetId -&gt; (string) The sheet ID of the tooltip sheet that is used by the tooltip. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ DataLabelOptions -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the presentation of the data labels. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility option that determines if data labels are displayed. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE CategoryLabelVisibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the category labels within the data labels. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE MeasureLabelVisibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the measure labels within the data labels. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE Position -&gt; (string) Determines the positioning of the data label relative to a section of the fun- nel. Possible values: o INSIDE o OUTSIDE o LEFT o TOP o BOTTOM o RIGHT LabelFontConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The font configuration for the data la- bels. Only the FontSize attribute of the font configuration is used for data labels. FontSize -&gt; (structure) The option that determines the text display size. Relative -&gt; (string) The lexical name for the text size, proportional to its sur- rounding context. Possible values: o EXTRA_SMALL o SMALL o MEDIUM o LARGE o EXTRA_LARGE Absolute -&gt; (string) The font size that you want to use in px. FontDecoration -&gt; (string) Determines the appearance of decora- tive lines on the text. Possible values: o UNDERLINE o NONE FontColor -&gt; (string) Determines the color of the text. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}$ FontWeight -&gt; (structure) The option that determines the text display weight, or boldness. Name -&gt; (string) The lexical name for the level of boldness of the text display. Possible values: o NORMAL o BOLD FontStyle -&gt; (string) Determines the text display face that is inherited by the given font family. Possible values: o NORMAL o ITALIC FontFamily -&gt; (string) The font family that you want to use. 