ue format configu- ration. NullString -&gt; (string) [re- quired] Determines the null string of null values. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 CalculatedMeasureField -&gt; (struc- ture) The calculated measure field only used in pivot tables. FieldId -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The custom field ID. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 Expression -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The expression in the ta- ble calculation. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 4096 SortConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The sort configuration of a word cloud vi- sual. CategoryItemsLimit -&gt; (structure) The limit on the number of groups that are displayed in a word cloud. ItemsLimit -&gt; (long) The limit on how many items of a field are showed in the chart. For example, the number of slices that are displayed in a pie chart. OtherCategories -&gt; (string) The Show other of an axis in the chart. Choose one of the following options: o INCLUDE o EXCLUDE Possible values: o INCLUDE o EXCLUDE CategorySort -&gt; (list) The sort configuration of group by fields. Constraints: o max: 100 (structure) The field sort options in a chart configuration. FieldSort -&gt; (structure) The sort configuration for a field in a field well. FieldId -&gt; (string) [required] The sort configuration target field. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 Direction -&gt; (string) [required] The sort direction. Choose one of the following options: o ASC : Ascending o DESC : Descending Possible values: o ASC o DESC ColumnSort -&gt; (structure) The sort configuration for a col- umn that is not used in a field well. SortBy -&gt; (structure) [required] A column of a data set. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the col- umn belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The name of the column. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Direction -&gt; (string) [required] The sort direction. Possible values: o ASC o DESC AggregationFunction -&gt; (struc- ture) The aggregation function that is defined in the column sort. NumericalAggregationFunction -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for numerical values. SimpleNumericalAggregation -&gt; (string) Built-in aggregation functions for numeri- cal values. o SUM : The sum of a dimension or mea- sure. o AVERAGE : The aver- age of a dimension or measure. o MIN : The minimum value of a dimension or measure. o MAX : The maximum value of a dimension or measure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or mea- sure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of distinct values in a dimen- sion or measure. o VAR : The variance of a dimension or measure. o VARP : The parti- tioned variance of a dimension or mea- sure. o STDEV : The standard deviation of a di- mension or measure. o STDEVP : The parti- tioned standard de- viation of a dimen- sion or measure. o MEDIAN : The median value of a dimension or measure. Possible values: o SUM o AVERAGE o MIN o MAX o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o VAR o VARP o STDEV o STDEVP o MEDIAN PercentileAggregation -&gt; (structure) An aggregation based on the percentile of values in a dimension or measure. PercentileValue -&gt; (double) The percentile value. This value can be any numeric constant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the me- dian value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 CategoricalAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (string) Aggregation for categori- cal values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Aggre- gate by the total number of distinct values. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT DateAggregationFunction -&gt; (string) Aggregation for date val- ues. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Aggre- gate by the total number of distinct values. o MIN : Select the small- est date value. o MAX : Select the largest date value. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o MIN o MAX AttributeAggregationFunction -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for attrib- utes. SimpleAttributeAggregation -&gt; (string) The built-in aggrega- tion functions for at- tributes. o UNIQUE_VALUE : Re- turns the unique value for a field, aggregated by the dimension fields. Possible values: o UNIQUE_VALUE ValueForMultipleValues -&gt; (string) Used by the UNIQUE_VALUE aggrega- tion function. If there are multiple values for the field used by the aggrega- tion, the value for this property will be returned instead. De- faults to '*'. CategoryLabelOptions -&gt; (structure) The label options (label text, label visi- bility, and sort icon visibility) for the word cloud category. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of an axis label on a chart. Choose one of the following op- tions: o VISIBLE : Shows the axis. o HIDDEN : Hides the axis. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE SortIconVisibility -&gt; (string) The visibility configuration of the sort icon on a chart's axis label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE AxisLabelOptions -&gt; (list) The label options for a chart axis. Constraints: o max: 100 (structure) The label options for a chart axis. You must specify the field that the label is targeted to. FontConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The font configuration of the axis label. FontSize -&gt; (structure) The option that determines the text display size. Relative -&gt; (string) The lexical name for the text size, proportional to its surrounding context. Possible values: o EXTRA_SMALL o SMALL o MEDIUM o LARGE o EXTRA_LARGE Absolute -&gt; (string) The font size that you want to use in px. FontDecoration -&gt; (string) Determines the appearance of decorative lines on the text. Possible values: o UNDERLINE o NONE FontColor -&gt; (string) Determines the color of the text. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}$ FontWeight -&gt; (structure) The option that determines the text display weight, or boldness. Name -&gt; (string) The lexical name for the level of boldness of the text display. Possible values: o NORMAL o BOLD FontStyle -&gt; (string) Determines the text display face that is inherited by the given font family. Possible values: o NORMAL o ITALIC FontFamily -&gt; (string) The font family that you want to use. Constraints: o max: 256 CustomLabel -&gt; (string) The text for the axis label. ApplyTo -&gt; (structure) The options that indicate which field the label belongs to. FieldId -&gt; (string) [required] The field that the axis label is targeted to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 Column -&gt; (structure) [required] The column that the axis la- bel is targeted to. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the col- umn belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The name of the column. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 WordCloudOptions -&gt; (structure) The options for a word cloud visual. WordOrientation -&gt; (string) The word orientation options (horizon- tal, horizontal_and_vertical) for the words in a word cloud. Possible values: o HORIZONTAL o HORIZONTAL_AND_VERTICAL WordScaling -&gt; (string) The word scaling options (emphasize, normal) for the words in a word cloud. Possible values: o EMPHASIZE o NORMAL CloudLayout -&gt; (string) The cloud layout options (fluid, normal) of a word cloud. Possible values: o FLUID o NORMAL WordCasing -&gt; (string) The word casing options (lower_case, ex- isting_case) for the words in a word cloud. Possible values: o LOWER_CASE o EXISTING_CASE WordPadding -&gt; (string) The word padding options (none, small, medium, large) for the words in a word cloud. Possible values: o NONE o SMALL o MEDIUM o LARGE MaximumStringLength -&gt; (integer) The length limit of each word from 1-100. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 100 Interactions -&gt; (structure) The general visual interactions setup for a visual. VisualMenuOption -&gt; (structure) The on-visual menu options for a visual. AvailabilityStatus -&gt; (string) The availaiblity status of a vi- sual's menu options. Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED ContextMenuOption -&gt; (structure) The context menu options for a visual. AvailabilityStatus -&gt; (string) The availability status of the con- text menu options. If the value of this property is set to ENABLED , dashboard readers can interact with the context menu. Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED Actions -&gt; (list) The list of custom actions that are configured for a visual. Constraints: o max: 10 (structure) A custom action defined on a visual. CustomActionId -&gt; (string) [required] The ID of the VisualCustomAction . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the VisualCustomAction . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 256 Status -&gt; (string) The status of the VisualCustomAction . Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED Trigger -&gt; (string) [required] The trigger of the VisualCustomAction . Valid values are defined as follows: o DATA_POINT_CLICK : Initiates a custom action by a left pointer click on a data point. o DATA_POINT_MENU : Initiates a custom action by right pointer click from the menu. Possible values: o DATA_POINT_CLICK o DATA_POINT_MENU ActionOperations -&gt; (list) [required] A list of VisualCustomActionOperations . This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2 (structure) The operation that is defined by the custom action. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. FilterOperation -&gt; (structure) The filter operation that filters data included in a visual or in an entire sheet. SelectedFieldsConfiguration -&gt; (structure) [required] The configuration that chooses the fields to be fil- tered. SelectedFields -&gt; (list) Chooses the fields that are filtered in CustomAc- tionFilterOperation . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 20 (string) Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 SelectedFieldOptions -&gt; (string) A structure that contains the options that choose which fields are filtered in the CustomActionFilter- Operation . Valid values are defined as follows: o ALL_FIELDS : Applies the filter operation to all fields. Possible values: o ALL_FIELDS SelectedColumns -&gt; (list) The selected columns of a dataset. Constraints: o max: 10 (structure) A column of a data set. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the column. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 TargetVisualsConfiguration -&gt; (structure) [required] The configuration that chooses the target visuals to be filtered. SameSheetTargetVisualConfigu- ration -&gt; (structure) The configuration of the same-sheet target visuals that you want to be fil- tered. TargetVisuals -&gt; (list) A list of the target visual IDs that are located in the same sheet of the analysis. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 75 (string) Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ TargetVisualOptions -&gt; (string) The options that choose the target vi- sual in the same sheet. Valid values are de- fined as follows: o ALL_VISUALS : Ap- plies the filter op- eration to all visu- als in the same sheet. Possible values: o ALL_VISUALS NavigationOperation -&gt; (structure) The navigation operation that navigates between different sheets in the same analysis. LocalNavigationConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The configuration that chooses the navigation tar- get. TargetSheetId -&gt; (string) [required] The sheet that is targeted for navigation in the same analysis. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ URLOperation -&gt; (structure) The URL operation that opens a link to another webpage. URLTemplate -&gt; (string) [re- quired] THe URL link of the