gation for numerical values. SimpleNumericalAggregation -&gt; (string) Built-in aggregation functions for numeri- cal values. o SUM : The sum of a dimension or mea- sure. o AVERAGE : The aver- age of a dimension or measure. o MIN : The minimum value of a dimension or measure. o MAX : The maximum value of a dimension or measure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or mea- sure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of distinct values in a dimen- sion or measure. o VAR : The variance of a dimension or measure. o VARP : The parti- tioned variance of a dimension or mea- sure. o STDEV : The standard deviation of a di- mension or measure. o STDEVP : The parti- tioned standard de- viation of a dimen- sion or measure. o MEDIAN : The median value of a dimension or measure. Possible values: o SUM o AVERAGE o MIN o MAX o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o VAR o VARP o STDEV o STDEVP o MEDIAN PercentileAggregation -&gt; (structure) An aggregation based on the percentile of values in a dimension or measure. PercentileValue -&gt; (double) The percentile value. This value can be any numeric constant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the me- dian value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 CategoricalAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (string) Aggregation for categori- cal values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Aggre- gate by the total number of distinct values. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT DateAggregationFunction -&gt; (string) Aggregation for date val- ues. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Aggre- gate by the total number of distinct values. o MIN : Select the small- est date value. o MAX : Select the largest date value. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o MIN o MAX AttributeAggregationFunction -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for attrib- utes. SimpleAttributeAggregation -&gt; (string) The built-in aggrega- tion functions for at- tributes. o UNIQUE_VALUE : Re- turns the unique value for a field, aggregated by the dimension fields. Possible values: o UNIQUE_VALUE ValueForMultipleValues -&gt; (string) Used by the UNIQUE_VALUE aggrega- tion function. If there are multiple values for the field used by the aggrega- tion, the value for this property will be returned instead. De- faults to '*'. SourceItemsLimit -&gt; (structure) The limit on the number of source nodes that are displayed in a sankey diagram. ItemsLimit -&gt; (long) The limit on how many items of a field are showed in the chart. For example, the number of slices that are displayed in a pie chart. OtherCategories -&gt; (string) The Show other of an axis in the chart. Choose one of the following options: o INCLUDE o EXCLUDE Possible values: o INCLUDE o EXCLUDE DestinationItemsLimit -&gt; (structure) The limit on the number of destination nodes that are displayed in a sankey di- agram. ItemsLimit -&gt; (long) The limit on how many items of a field are showed in the chart. For example, the number of slices that are displayed in a pie chart. OtherCategories -&gt; (string) The Show other of an axis in the chart. Choose one of the following options: o INCLUDE o EXCLUDE Possible values: o INCLUDE o EXCLUDE DataLabels -&gt; (structure) The data label configuration of a sankey diagram. Visibility -&gt; (string) Determines the visibility of the data labels. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE CategoryLabelVisibility -&gt; (string) Determines the visibility of the cate- gory field labels. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE MeasureLabelVisibility -&gt; (string) Determines the visibility of the measure field labels. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE DataLabelTypes -&gt; (list) The option that determines the data la- bel type. Constraints: o max: 100 (structure) The option that determines the data label type. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. FieldLabelType -&gt; (structure) Determines the label configura- tion for the entire field. FieldId -&gt; (string) Indicates the field that is targeted by the field label. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the field label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE DataPathLabelType -&gt; (structure) The option that specifies indi- vidual data values for labels. FieldId -&gt; (string) The field ID of the field that the data label needs to be applied to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 FieldValue -&gt; (string) The actual value of the field that is labeled. Constraints: o max: 2048 Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the data label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE RangeEndsLabelType -&gt; (structure) Determines the label configura- tion for range end value in a vi- sual. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the range ends label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE MinimumLabelType -&gt; (structure) Determines the label configura- tion for the minimum value in a visual. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the minimum label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE MaximumLabelType -&gt; (structure) Determines the label configura- tion for the maximum value in a visual. Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the maximum label. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE Position -&gt; (string) Determines the position of the data la- bels. Possible values: o INSIDE o OUTSIDE o LEFT o TOP o BOTTOM o RIGHT LabelContent -&gt; (string) Determines the content of the data la- bels. Possible values: o VALUE o PERCENT o VALUE_AND_PERCENT LabelFontConfiguration -&gt; (structure) Determines the font configuration of the data labels. FontSize -&gt; (structure) The option that determines the text display size. Relative -&gt; (string) The lexical name for the text size, proportional to its sur- rounding context. Possible values: o EXTRA_SMALL o SMALL o MEDIUM o LARGE o EXTRA_LARGE Absolute -&gt; (string) The font size that you want to use in px. FontDecoration -&gt; (string) Determines the appearance of decora- tive lines on the text. Possible values: o UNDERLINE o NONE FontColor -&gt; (string) Determines the color of the text. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}$ FontWeight -&gt; (structure) The option that determines the text display weight, or boldness. Name -&gt; (string) The lexical name for the level of boldness of the text display. Possible values: o NORMAL o BOLD FontStyle -&gt; (string) Determines the text display face that is inherited by the given font family. Possible values: o NORMAL o ITALIC FontFamily -&gt; (string) The font family that you want to use. Constraints: o max: 256 LabelColor -&gt; (string) Determines the color of the data labels. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}$ Overlap -&gt; (string) Determines whether overlap is enabled or disabled for the data labels. Possible values: o DISABLE_OVERLAP o ENABLE_OVERLAP TotalsVisibility -&gt; (string) Determines the visibility of the total. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE Interactions -&gt; (structure) The general visual interactions setup for a visual. VisualMenuOption -&gt; (structure) The on-visual menu options for a visual. AvailabilityStatus -&gt; (string) The availaiblity status of a vi- sual's menu options. Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED ContextMenuOption -&gt; (structure) The context menu options for a visual. AvailabilityStatus -&gt; (string) The availability status of the con- text menu options. If the value of this property is set to ENABLED , dashboard readers can interact with the context menu. Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED Actions -&gt; (list) The list of custom actions that are configured for a visual. Constraints: o max: 10 (structure) A custom action defined on a visual. CustomActionId -&gt; (string) [required] The ID of the VisualCustomAction . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the VisualCustomAction . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 256 Status -&gt; (string) The status of the VisualCustomAction . Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED Trigger -&gt; (string) [required] The trigger of the VisualCustomAction . Valid values are defined as follows: o DATA_POINT_CLICK : Initiates a custom action by a left pointer click on a data point. o DATA_POINT_MENU : Initiates a custom action by right pointer click from the menu. Possible values: o DATA_POINT_CLICK o DATA_POINT_MENU ActionOperations -&gt; (list) [required] A list of VisualCustomActionOperations . This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2 (structure) The operation that is defined by the custom action. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. FilterOperation -&gt; (structure) The filter operation that filters data included in a visual or in an entire sheet. SelectedFieldsConfiguration -&gt; (structure) [required] The configuration that chooses the fields to be fil- tered. SelectedFields -&gt; (list) Chooses the fields that are filtered in CustomAc- tionFilterOperation . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 20 (string) Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 SelectedFieldOptions -&gt; (string) A structure that contains the options that choose which fields are filtered in the CustomActionFilter- Operation . Valid values are defined as follows: o ALL_FIELDS : Applies the filter operation to all fields. Possible values: o ALL_FIELDS SelectedColumns -&gt; (list) The selected columns of a dataset. Constraints: o max: 10 (structure) A column of a data set. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the column. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 TargetVisualsConfiguration -&gt; (structure) [required] The configuration that chooses the target visu