n- figuration. Possible values: o POSITIVE o NEGATIVE NullValueFormatCon- figuration -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the null value format configu- ration. NullString -&gt; (string) [re- quired] Determines the null string of null values. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 PercentageDisplayFor- matConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the per- centage display format configura- tion. Prefix -&gt; (string) Determines the prefix value of the percentage format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Suffix -&gt; (string) Determines the suffix value of the percentage format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 SeparatorConfigura- tion -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the numeric separator con- figuration. DecimalSepara- tor -&gt; (string) Determines the decimal separator. Possible values: o COMMA o DOT o SPACE ThousandsSepa- rator -&gt; (structure) The options that deter- mine the thousands separator configura- tion. Symbol -&gt; (string) Deter- mines the thou- sands separa- tor sym- bol. Possible values: o COMMA o DOT o SPACE Visibility -&gt; (string) Deter- mines the vis- ibility of the thou- sands separa- tor. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISI- BLE Group- ingStyle -&gt; (string) Deter- mines the way numbers are styled to ac- commo- date differ- ent read- ability stan- dards. The DE- FAULT value uses the standard interna- tional grouping system and groups numbers by the thou- sands. The LAKHS value uses the Indian number- ing sys- tem and groups numbers by lakhs and crores. Possible values: o DE- FAULT o LAKHS DecimalPlacesCon- figuration -&gt; (structure) The option that determines the decimal places configuration. DecimalPlaces -&gt; (long) [re- quired] The values of the deci- mal places. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 20 NegativeValueCon- figuration -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the negative value configu- ration. DisplayMode -&gt; (string) [re- quired] Determines the display mode of the negative value con- figuration. Possible values: o POSITIVE o NEGATIVE NullValueFormatCon- figuration -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the null value format configu- ration. NullString -&gt; (string) [re- quired] Determines the null string of null values. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 VisualOptions -&gt; (structure) The persisted properties of the plugin vi- sual. VisualProperties -&gt; (list) The persisted properties and their val- ues. (structure) The key value pair of the persisted property. Name -&gt; (string) The name of the plugin visual property. Value -&gt; (string) The value of the plugin visual property. SortConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The sort configuration of the plugin vi- sual. PluginVisualTableQuerySort -&gt; (structure) The table query sorting options for the plugin visual. RowSort -&gt; (list) Determines how data is sorted in the response. Constraints: o max: 100 (structure) The field sort options in a chart configuration. FieldSort -&gt; (structure) The sort configuration for a field in a field well. FieldId -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The sort configuration target field. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 Direction -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The sort direction. Choose one of the following op- tions: o ASC : Ascending o DESC : Descending Possible values: o ASC o DESC ColumnSort -&gt; (structure) The sort configuration for a column that is not used in a field well. SortBy -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] A column of a data set. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the col- umn. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Direction -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The sort direction. Possible values: o ASC o DESC AggregationFunction -&gt; (structure) The aggregation function that is defined in the column sort. NumericalAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for numer- ical values. SimpleNumericalAggre- gation -&gt; (string) Built-in aggrega- tion functions for numerical values. o SUM : The sum of a dimension or measure. o AVERAGE : The av- erage of a dimen- sion or measure. o MIN : The minimum value of a dimen- sion or measure. o MAX : The maximum value of a dimen- sion or measure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or measure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of dis- tinct values in a dimension or mea- sure. o VAR : The vari- ance of a dimen- sion or measure. o VARP : The parti- tioned variance of a dimension or measure. o STDEV : The stan- dard deviation of a dimension or measure. o STDEVP : The par- titioned standard deviation of a dimension or mea- sure. o MEDIAN : The me- dian value of a dimension or mea- sure. Possible values: o SUM o AVERAGE o MIN o MAX o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o VAR o VARP o STDEV o STDEVP o MEDIAN PercentileAggregation -&gt; (structure) An aggregation based on the per- centile of values in a dimension or measure. PercentileValue -&gt; (double) The percentile value. This value can be any numeric constant 0100. A percentile value of 50 computes the median value of the measure. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 100 CategoricalAggregation- Function -&gt; (string) Aggregation for cate- gorical values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Ag- gregate by the total number of distinct values. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT DateAggregationFunction -&gt; (string) Aggregation for date values. o COUNT : Aggregate by the total number of values, including duplicates. o DISTINCT_COUNT : Ag- gregate by the total number of distinct values. o MIN : Select the smallest date value. o MAX : Select the largest date value. Possible values: o COUNT o DISTINCT_COUNT o MIN o MAX AttributeAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for at- tributes. SimpleAttributeAggre- gation -&gt; (string) The built-in aggre- gation functions for attributes. o UNIQUE_VALUE : Returns the unique value for a field, aggre- gated by the di- mension fields. Possible values: o UNIQUE_VALUE ValueForMultipleValues -&gt; (string) Used by the UNIQUE_VALUE aggre- gation function. If there are multiple values for the field used by the aggregation, the value for this property will be returned instead. Defaults to '*'. ItemsLimitConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The maximum amount of data to be re- turned by a query. ItemsLimit -&gt; (long) Determines how many values are be fetched at once. Actions -&gt; (list) The list of custom actions that are configured for a visual. Constraints: o max: 10 (structure) A custom action defined on a visual. CustomActionId -&gt; (string) [required] The ID of the VisualCustomAction . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the VisualCustomAction . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 256 Status -&gt; (string) The status of the VisualCustomAction . Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED Trigger -&gt; (string) [required] The trigger of the VisualCustomAction . Valid values are defined as follows: o DATA_POINT_CLICK : Initiates a custom action by a left pointer click on a data point. o DATA_POINT_MENU : Initiates a custom action by right pointer click from the menu. Possible values: o DATA_POINT_CLICK o DATA_POINT_MENU ActionOperations -&gt; (list) [required] A list of VisualCustomActionOperations . This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2 (structure) The operation that is defined by the custom action. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. FilterOperation -&gt; (structure) The filter operation that filters data included in a visual or in an entire sheet. SelectedFieldsConfiguration -&gt; (structure) [required] The configuration that chooses the fields to be fil- tered. SelectedFields -&gt; (list) Chooses