pens a link to another webpage. URLTemplate -&gt; (string) [re- quired] THe URL link of the CustomAc- tionURLOperation . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 URLTarget -&gt; (string) [required] The target of the CustomAc- tionURLOperation . Valid values are defined as follows: o NEW_TAB : Opens the target URL in a new browser tab. o NEW_WINDOW : Opens the tar- get URL in a new browser window. o SAME_TAB : Opens the target URL in the same browser tab. Possible values: o NEW_TAB o NEW_WINDOW o SAME_TAB SetParametersOperation -&gt; (struc- ture) The set parameter operation that sets parameters in custom action. ParameterValueConfigurations -&gt; (list) [required] The parameter that determines the value configuration. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 200 (structure) The configuration of adding parameters in ac- tion. DestinationParameterName -&gt; (string) [required] The destination para- meter name of the Set- ParameterValueConfigu- ration . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 o pattern: ^[a-zA-Z0-9]+$ Value -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] The configuration of destination parameter values. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the at- tributes can be de- fined. CustomValuesConfigura- tion -&gt; (structure) The configuration of custom values for destination pa- rameter in Destina- tionParameterValue- Configuration . IncludeNullValue -&gt; (boolean) Includes the null value in custom action parameter val- ues. CustomValues -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] The customized parameter val- ues. This is a union type structure. For this struc- ture to be valid, only one of the attrib- utes can be de- fined. StringValues -&gt; (list) A list of string-type parameter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (string) IntegerValues -&gt; (list) A list of integer-type parameter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (long) DecimalValues -&gt; (list) A list of decimal-type parameter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (double) DateTimeValues -&gt; (list) A list of date- time-type parameter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (timestamp) SelectAllValueOptions -&gt; (string) The configuration that selects all options. Possible values: o ALL_VALUES SourceParameterName -&gt; (string) The source parame- ter name of the destination parame- ter. SourceField -&gt; (string) The source field ID of the destination parameter. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 SourceColumn -&gt; (structure) A column of a data set. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column be- longs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the column. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 VisualContentAltText -&gt; (string) The alt text for the visual. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1024 TextBoxes -&gt; (list) The text boxes that are on a tooltip sheet. Constraints: o max: 5 (structure) A text box. SheetTextBoxId -&gt; (string) [required] The unique identifier for a text box. This identi- fier must be unique within the context of a dash- board, template, or analysis. Two dashboards, analyses, or templates can have text boxes that share identifiers. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Content -&gt; (string) The content that is displayed in the text box. Constraints: o max: 150000 Interactions -&gt; (structure) The general textbox interactions setup for a textbox. TextBoxMenuOption -&gt; (structure) The menu options for the textbox. AvailabilityStatus -&gt; (string) The availability status of the textbox menu. If the value of this property is set to ENABLED , dashboard readers can interact with the textbox menu. Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED Images -&gt; (list) A list of images on a tooltip sheet. Constraints: o max: 5 (structure) An image that is located on a sheet. SheetImageId -&gt; (string) [required] The ID of the sheet image. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Source -&gt; (structure) [required] The source of the image. SheetImageStaticFileSource -&gt; (structure) The source of the static file that contains the image. StaticFileId -&gt; (string) [required] The ID of the static file that contains the image. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Scaling -&gt; (structure) Determines how the image is scaled. ScalingType -&gt; (string) The scaling option to use when fitting the im- age inside the container. Valid values are defined as follows: o SCALE_TO_WIDTH : The image takes up the en- tire width of the container. The image aspect ratio is preserved. o SCALE_TO_HEIGHT : The image takes up the en- tire height of the container. The image as- pect ratio is preserved. o SCALE_TO_CONTAINER : The image takes up the entire width and height of the container. The image aspect ratio is not preserved. o SCALE_NONE : The image is displayed in its original size and is not scaled to the con- tainer. Possible values: o SCALE_TO_WIDTH o SCALE_TO_HEIGHT o SCALE_TO_CONTAINER o SCALE_NONE Tooltip -&gt; (structure) The tooltip to be shown when hovering over the im- age. TooltipText -&gt; (structure) The text that appears in the tooltip. PlainText -&gt; (string) The plain text format. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1024 Visibility -&gt; (string) The visibility of the tooltip. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE ImageContentAltText -&gt; (string) The alt text for the image. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1024 Interactions -&gt; (structure) The general image interactions setup for an image. ImageMenuOption -&gt; (structure) The menu options for the image. AvailabilityStatus -&gt; (string) The availability status of the image menu. If the value of this property is set to EN- ABLED , dashboard readers can interact with the image menu. Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED Actions -&gt; (list) A list of custom actions that are configured for an image. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 10 (structure) A custom action defined on an image. CustomActionId -&gt; (string) [required] The ID of the custom action. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ Name -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the custom action. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 256 Status -&gt; (string) The status of the custom action. Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED Trigger -&gt; (string) [required] The trigger of the VisualCustomAction . Valid values are defined as follows: o CLICK : Initiates a custom action by a left pointer click on a data point. o MENU : Initiates a custom action by right pointer click from the menu. Possible values: o CLICK o MENU ActionOperations -&gt; (list) [required] A list of ImageCustomActionOperations . This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the at- tributes can be defined. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2 (structure) The operation that is defined by the custom action. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. NavigationOperation -&gt; (structure) The navigation operation that navi- gates between different sheets in the same analysis. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. LocalNavigationConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The configuration that chooses the navigation target. TargetSheetId -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The sheet that is targeted for navigation in the same analysis. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ URLOperation -&gt; (structure) The URL operation that opens a link to another webpage. URLTemplate -&gt; (string) [required] THe URL link of the CustomAc- tionURLOperation . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 URLTarget -&gt; (string) [required] The target of the CustomActionUR- LOperation . Valid values are defined as fol- lows: o NEW_TAB : Opens the target URL in a new browser tab. o NEW_WINDOW : Opens the target URL in a new browser window. o SAME_TAB : Opens the target URL in the same browser tab. Possible values: o NEW_TAB o NEW_WINDOW o SAME_TAB SetParametersOperation -&gt; (structure) The set parameter operation that sets parameters in custom action. ParameterValueConfigurations -&gt; (list) [required] The parameter that determines the value configuration. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 200 (structure) The configuration of adding parameters in action. DestinationParameterName -&gt; (string) [required] The destination parameter name of the SetParameter- ValueConfiguration . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 o pattern: ^[a-zA-Z0-9]+$ Value -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] The configuration of des- tination parameter values. This is a union type structure. For this struc- ture to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. CustomValuesConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The configuration of custom values for des- tination parameter in DestinationParameter- ValueConfiguration . IncludeNullValue -&gt; (boolean) Includes the null value in custom ac- tion parameter val- ues. CustomValues -&gt; (structure) [required] The customized pa- rameter values. This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. StringValues -&gt; (list) A list of string-type pa- rameter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (string) IntegerValues -&gt; (list) A list of inte- ger-type para- meter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (long) DecimalValues -&gt; (list) A list of deci- mal-type para- meter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (double) DateTimeValues -&gt; (list) A list of date- time-type para- meter values. Constraints: o max: 50000 (timestamp) SelectAllValueOptions -&gt; (string) The configuration that selects all options. Possible values: o ALL_VALUES SourceParameterName -&gt; (string) The source parameter name of the destina- tion parameter. SourceField -&gt; (string) The source field ID of the destination para- meter. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 SourceColumn -&gt; (struc- ture) A column of a data set. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the column. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 Layouts -&gt; (list) Layouts define how the components of a tooltip sheet are arranged. For more information, see Types of layout in the Amazon Quick Suite User Guide . Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 1 (structure) A Layout defines the placement of elements within a sheet. For more information, see Types of layout in the Ama- zon Quick Suite User Guide . This is a union type structure. For this structure to be valid, only one of the attributes can be defined. Configuration -&gt; (structure) [required] The configuration that determines what the type of layout for a sheet. GridLayout -&gt; (structure) A type of layout that can be used on a sheet. In a grid layout, visuals snap to a grid with standard spacing and alignment. Dashboards are displayed as designed, with options to fit to screen or view at actual size. A grid layout can be configured to behave in one of two ways when the viewport is resized: FIXED or RESPON- SIVE . Elements -&gt; (list) [required] The elements that are included in a grid layout. Constraints: o max: 430 (structure) An element within a grid layout. ElementId -&gt; (string) [required] A unique identifier for an element within a grid layout. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 512 o pattern: [\w\-]+ ElementType -&gt; (string) [required] The type of element. Possible values: o VISUAL o FILTER_CONTROL o PARAMETER_CONTROL o TEXT_BOX o IMAGE ColumnIndex -&gt; (integer) The column index for the upper left corner of an element. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 35 ColumnSpan -&gt; (integer) [required] The width of a grid element ex- pressed as a number of grid columns. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 36 RowIndex -&gt; (integer) The row index for the upper left corner of an element. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 9009 RowSpan -&