- ture) The sort configuration for user-specified values in the control. Use this option to sort values that are manually entered by users in a drop- down or list control. Direction -&gt; (string) [re- quired] The sort direction for the selectable values. Choose one of the following op- tions: o ASC : Sort in ascending order. o DESC : Sort in descend- ing order. o USER_DEFINED_ORDER : Preserve the order in which the values were entered. Possible values: o ASC o DESC o USER_DEFINED_ORDER ControlColumnSort -&gt; (structure) The sort configuration for controls that are tied to a dataset column. Use this op- tion to sort control values by an aggregate of a column. Column -&gt; (structure) [re- quired] The column that determines the sort order of aggre- gated values. DataSetIdentifier -&gt; (string) The data set that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 2048 TopicIdentifier -&gt; (string) The topic that the column belongs to. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 2048 ColumnName -&gt; (string) [required] The name of the col- umn. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 128 SortDirection -&gt; (string) [required] The sort direction of val- ues. o ASC : Sort in ascending order. o DESC : Sort in descend- ing order. Possible values: o ASC o DESC AggregationFunction -&gt; (structure) The function that aggre- gates the values in Column . NumericalAggregationFunc- tion -&gt; (structure) Aggregation for numer- ical values. SimpleNumericalAggre- gation -&gt; (string) Built-in aggrega- tion functions for numerical values. o SUM : The sum of a dimension or measure. o AVERAGE : The av- erage of a dimen- sion or measure. o MIN : The minimum value of a dimen- sion or measure. o MAX : The maximum value of a dimen- sion or measure. o COUNT : The count of a dimension or measure. o DISTINCT_COUNT : The count of dis- tinct values in a dimension or mea- sure. o VAR : The vari- ance of a dimen- sion or measure. o VARP : The parti- tioned variance of a dimension or measure. o STDEV : The stan- dar