straints: o max: 2048 Color -&gt; (string) [required] The color that is applied to the data value. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}$ SpecialValue -&gt; (string) The value of a special data value. Possible values: o EMPTY o NULL o OTHER DecalSettingsConfiguration -&gt; (structure) Decal configuration of the column. CustomDecalSettings -&gt; (list) A list of up to 50 decal settings. Constraints: o max: 50 (structure) Decal settings for accessibility features that de- fine visual patterns and styling for data ele- ments. ElementValue -&gt; (string) Field value of the field that you are setting the decal pattern to. Applicable only for field level settings. Constraints: o max: 1024 DecalVisibility -&gt; (string) Visibility setting for the decal pattern. Possible values: o HIDDEN o VISIBLE DecalColor -&gt; (string) Color configuration for the decal pattern. Constraints: o pattern: ^#[A-F0-9]{6}(?:[A-F0-9]{2})?$ DecalPatternType -&gt; (string) Type of pattern used for the decal, such as solid, diagonal, or circular patterns in vari- ous sizes. o SOLID : Solid fill pattern. o DIAGONAL_SMALL : Small diagonal stripes pat- tern. o DIAGONAL_MEDIUM : Medium diagonal stripes pattern. o DIAGONAL_LARGE : Large diagonal stripes pat- tern. o DIAGONAL_OPPOSITE_SMALL : Small cross-diago- nal stripes pattern. o DIAGONAL_OPPOSITE_MEDIUM : Medium cross-diag- onal stripes pattern. o DIAGONAL_OPPOSITE_LARGE : Large cross-diago- nal stripes pattern. o CIRCLE_SMALL : Small circle pattern. o CIRCLE_MEDIUM : Medium circle pattern. o CIRCLE_LARGE : Large circle pattern. o DIAMOND_SMALL : Small diamonds pattern. o DIAMOND_MEDIUM : Medium diamonds pattern. o DIAMOND_LARGE : Large diamonds pattern. o DIAMOND_GRID_SMALL : Small diamond grid pat- tern. o DIAMOND_GRID_MEDIUM : Medium diamond grid pattern. o DIAMOND_GRID_LARGE : Large diamond grid pat- tern. o CHECKERBOARD_SMALL : Small checkerboard pat- tern. o CHECKERBOARD_MEDIUM : Medium checkerboard pattern. o CHECKERBOARD_LARGE : Large checkerboard pat- tern. o TRIANGLE_SMALL : Small triangles pattern. o TRIANGLE_MEDIUM : Medium triangles pattern. o TRIANGLE_LARGE : Large triangles pattern. Possible values: o SOLID o DIAGONAL_MEDIUM o CIRCLE_MEDIUM o DIAMOND_GRID_MEDIUM o CHECKERBOARD_MEDIUM o TRIANGLE_MEDIUM o DIAGONAL_OPPOSITE_MEDIUM o DIAMOND_MEDIUM o DIAGONAL_LARGE o CIRCLE_LARGE o DIAMOND_GRID_LARGE o CHECKERBOARD_LARGE o TRIANGLE_LARGE o DIAGONAL_OPPOSITE_LARGE o DIAMOND_LARGE o DIAGONAL_SMALL o CIRCLE_SMALL o DIAMOND_GRID_SMALL o CHECKERBOARD_SMALL o TRIANGLE_SMALL o DIAGONAL_OPPOSITE_SMALL o DIAMOND_SMALL DecalStyleType -&gt; (string) Style type for the decal, which can be either manual or automatic. This field is only applic- able for line series. o Manual : Apply manual line and marker config- uration for line series. o Auto : Apply automatic line and marker con- figuration for line series. Possible values: o Manual o Auto AnalysisDefaults -&gt; (structure) The configuration for default analysis settings. DefaultNewSheetConfiguration -&gt; (structure) [required] The configuration for default new sheet settings. InteractiveLayoutConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the default settings for in- teractive layout configuration. Grid -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the default settings for a grid layout configuration. CanvasSizeOptions -&gt; (structure) [required] Determines the screen canvas size options for a grid layout. ScreenCanvasSizeOptions -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the sizing of the canvas used in a grid layout. ResizeOption -&gt; (string) [required] This value determines the layout behavior when the viewport is resized. o FIXED : A fixed width will be used when optimizing the layout. In the Quick Sight console, this option is called Classic . o RESPONSIVE : The width of the canvas will be responsive and optimized to the view port. In the Quick Sight console, this option is called Tiled . Possible values: o FIXED o RESPONSIVE OptimizedViewPortWidth -&gt; (string) The width that the view port will be opti- mized for when the layout renders. FreeForm -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the default settings of a free-form layout configuration. CanvasSizeOptions -&gt; (structure) [required] Determines the screen canvas size options for a free-form layout. ScreenCanvasSizeOptions -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the sizing of the canvas used in a free-form layout. OptimizedViewPortWidth -&gt; (string) [required] The width that the view port will be opti- mized for when the layout renders. PaginatedLayoutConfiguration -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the default settings for a paginated layout configuration. SectionBased -&gt; (structure) The options that determine the default settings for a section-based layout configuration. CanvasSizeOptions -&gt; (structure) [required] Determines the screen canvas size options for a section-based layout. PaperCanvasSizeOptions -&gt; (structure) The options for a paper canvas of a sec- tion-based layout. PaperSize -&gt; (string) The paper size that is used to define can- vas dimensions. Possible values: o US_LETTER o US_LEGAL o US_TABLOID_LEDGER o A0 o A1 o A2 o A3 o A4 o A5 o JIS_B4 o JIS_B5 PaperOrientation -&gt; (string) The paper orientation that is used to de- fine canvas dimensions. Choose one of the following options: o PORTRAIT o LANDSCAPE Possible values: o PORTRAIT o LANDSCAPE PaperMargin -&gt; (structure) Defines the spacing between the canvas con- tent and the top, bottom, left, and right edges. Top -&gt; (string) Define the top spacing. Bottom -&gt; (string) Define the bottom spacing. Left -&gt; (string) Define the left spacing. Right -&gt; (string) Define the right spacing. SheetContentType -&gt; (string) The option that determines the sheet content type. Possible values: o PAGINATED o INTERACTIVE Options -&gt; (structure) An array of option definitions for a dashboard. Timezone -&gt; (string) Determines the timezone for